    "updated_at": "2025-09-12T08:35:34Z",
    "body": "Ok, I've added a [test](https://wpt.fyi/results/content-security-policy/generic/image-document-applies-csp.html?label=experimental&label=master&aligned) for subresources and turned @TimvdLippe's test into [tentative](https://wpt.fyi/results/content-security-policy/generic/image-document-ignores-csp-for-loading-main-image.tentative.html?label=experimental&label=master&aligned).\n\nIt seems that Firefox, Chrome and Safari all implement the same behavior. The difference with the html spec is that they don't refetch the image after loading the document. I guess it would make sense to adapt the spec, although it's not clear to me how to do that in an easy way.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
