    "updated_at": "2025-09-13T00:30:34Z",
    "body": "I think that sort of solution is neat, but I'd love to first hear what implementations do. I vaguely remember at least some of them don't follow the current spec in having the contents be `<img src=\"[the actual image URL]\">`, but instead do something like `<img src=\"internal:thisdocument\">` or maybe `<img src=\"data:...\">`.",
